# long_wait (D-932; 03 §11, 09 §9.4, §10.6): a twenty-minute wait in
# the square of the market town, with the levels the bundled game sets
# while the party rests. While the player waits a long wait, the tracts
# beyond the reach of its senses fall to cold: the far corner of the
# town is unloaded and its people are agents, following their routines;
# within sight of the square the stall keepers keep their stalls as
# before. The script's save-and-load mode saves and loads in the middle
# of the wait. When the wait is over the town loads again round the
# square, and the people of the far corner are where their routines put
# them at twenty-five past nine: at work.
use default seed=7
begin core:town_life place=1
advance 5s
assert "core:doing_near(@c:2140,1120,0, 30, 'at_home') > 0"
assert "core:doing_near(@self.loc, 60, 'keeping_stall') > 0"
as @self do { "wait": { "who": "self", "time": 1200 } }
advance 600s
assert "core:doing_near(@c:2140,1120,0, 30, 'working') + core:doing_near(@c:2140,1120,0, 30, 'at_home') == 0"
assert "core:doing_near(@self.loc, 60, 'keeping_stall') > 0"
advance 600s
assert "@self.loc.realm.time_of_day == 33605"
assert "core:doing_near(@c:2140,1120,0, 30, 'working') > 0"
expect hash bd8d3036ff8299df578922bb759da4f7
